('Escarabajo bombardero gigante', 'Giant Bombardier Beetle', 'Giant Bombardier Beetle', 'Alimaña', 'Alimaña mediana', 2.0, '2', '2d8+4 (13 pg)', '+0', '30 pies (6 casillas)', '16 (+6 natural), contacto 10, desprevenido 16', '+1/+2', 'Mordisco +2 cuerpo a cuerpo (1d4+1)', 'Mordisco +2 cuerpo a cuerpo (1d4+1)', '5 pies/5 pies', 'Ácido spray', 'Visión en la oscuridad 60 pies, rasgos de alimaña', 'Fort +5, Ref +0, Vol +0', 'Fue 13, Des 10, Con 14, Int Ø, Sab 10, Car 9', '—', '—', 'Bosques cálidos', 'Grupo (2-5) o click (6-11)', '', '', '3-4 DG (mediano); 5-6 DG (grande)', '—', 'These creatures feed primarily on carrion and offal, gathering heaps of the stuff in which to build nests and lay eggs. A giant bombardier beetle is about 6 feet long. Giant bombardier beetles normally attack only to defend themselves, their nests, or their eggs.

Acid Spray (Ex)
When attacked or disturbed, the creature can release a 10-foot cone of acidic vapor once per round. Those within the cone must succeed on a DC 13 Fortitude save or take 1d4+2 points of acid damage. The save DC is Constitution-based.', 'criatura'),
('Escarabajo de fuego gigante', 'Giant Fire Beetle', 'Giant Fire Beetle', 'Alimaña', 'Alimaña pequeña', 0.333, '1/3', '1d8 (4 pg)', '+0', '30 pies (6 casillas)', '16 (+1 tamaño, +5 natural), contacto 11, desprevenido 16', '+0/-4', 'Mordisco +1 cuerpo a cuerpo (2d4)', 'Mordisco +1 cuerpo a cuerpo (2d4)', '5 pies/5 pies', '—', 'Visión en la oscuridad 60 pies, rasgos de alimaña', 'Fort +2, Ref +0, Vol +0', 'Fue 10, Des 11, Con 11, Int Ø, Sab 10, Car 7', '—', '—', 'Llanuras cálidas', 'Grupo (2-5) o colonia (6-11)', '', 'Siempre neutral', '2-3 DG (pequeño)', '—', 'These luminous nocturnal insects are prized by miners and adventurers. They have two glands, one above each eye, that produce a red glow. The glands’ luminosity persists for 1d6 days after removal from the beetle, illuminating a roughly circular area with a 10-foot radius. Giant fire beetles are about 2 feet long.

